{
  "result": "Okay \u2014 just me thinking.\n\nI wouldn't directly choose world peace, or happiness. I'd choose something smaller that might lead there:\n\nI'd make curiosity kick in before fear.\n\nJust by a second. When we meet a stranger, a strange idea, a life that looks nothing like ours, our first reflex now is often to defend, dismiss, or decide. I'd tilt that \u2014 so the first impulse is *wait, what is it actually like to be you?*\n\nPeople would still disagree. They'd still argue, compete, make bad choices, grieve. I wouldn't want to erase any of that.\n\nBut so much cruelty seems to come from that instant moment where someone stops being a person and becomes a threat or a stereotype. If that moment were interrupted by genuine curiosity, just often enough...\n\nI think a lot of other things would quietly become possible.",
